    "final_text": "and derived the rest from it.\n- **Parts:** everything in the photo is there. That covers the posts with bead rows, finials, the pointed arch with teardrop, quatrefoil and rosette, and the round-arched lower tracery with thorns. Below the back are the bowed arms on round pads, fluted turned legs with bun feet, cusped arcade aprons and the box stretchers.\n- **Material:** a Poly Haven wood scan (CC0), recoloured to the photo's colours, with grime in the carving and wear on the seat and arm tops. It's baked into colour, roughness and normal maps.\n- **Measured match:** the silhouette overlap with your photo is 0.478, from the photo's camera angle. Part of the remaining gap is the photo's perspective, which I deliberately didn't copy into the geometry.\n\n**Review rounds:** seven, each read by a new reviewer who saw only images. The last one found nothing blocking. Along the way I fixed a real geometry bug: the front apron's arches had been filled in wrongly and looked torn. The arms took four rounds before they matched the photo.\n\n**Details simpler than the photo:**\n- The bead rows on the posts are sparser.\n- The finials are a bud with outward leaves rather than a full fleur-de-lis.\n- The arm pads are round discs, not rolled scrolls.\n- The arcade drops still look slightly pointed from a low angle.\n\n**Budget:** 9,984 triangles is twice the balanced tier's 5,000 top, the most the tier allows. It goes into the tracery and the turned parts, so I didn't decimate.\n\n**Storage:** you asked for compact storage, but I haven't deleted anything. The working files are still there: `review/` (285 MB), `textures/` (24 MB, the bakes and downloaded scans) and `optimize_tmp/` (12 MB). The bakes are also packed in the .blend, so none of these are needed. Should I delete them?\n\nI built this in your open Blender, which only held the empty startup scene; I removed its default cube first. Kiln Studio is running at http://127.0.0.1:4841/ if you want to look at the model there and pin notes on it.",
